volatility":0.10373663327919876,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":84.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.09225832842288345,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.024339346381410887,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":30.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.06891246039718069,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":59.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.01801124213114241,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":31.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.002605804146954327,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":46.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009149498234272824,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.19974001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Capital City Bank Group, Inc. operates as the financial holding company for Capital City Bank that provides a range of banking services to individual and corporate clients. The company offers financing for commercial business properties, equipment, inventories, and accounts receivable, as well as commercial leasing and letters of credit; treasury management services; and merchant credit card transaction processing services. It also provides commercial and residential real estate lending products, as well as fixed and adjustable-rate residential mortgage loans; personal, automobile, boat/RV, and home equity loans. In addition, the company offers institutional banking services, including customized checking and savings accounts, cash management systems, tax-exempt loans, lines of credit, and term loans to meet the needs of state and local governments, public schools and colleges, charities, membership, and not-for-profit associations. Further, it provides consumer banking services comprising checking accounts, savings programs, interactive/automated teller machines, debit/credit cards, night deposit services, safe deposit facilities, and online and mobile banking services. Additionally, the company provides asset management for individuals through agency, personal trust, IRA, and personal investment management accounts; and various retail investment products, such as the U.S. government bonds, tax-free municipal bonds, stocks, mutual funds, unit investment trusts, annuities, life insurance, and long-term health care, as well as business, estate, financial, insurance and business planning, tax planning, and asset protection advisory services. Further, the company offers mortgage banking. Capital City Bank Group, Inc. was founded in 1895 and is headquartered in Tallahassee, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William Godfrey Smith Jr. | Chairman & CEO | Age 72 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 902 people. Revenue per employee of $282K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $89K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Capital City Bank Group is a small-cap financial services business with a $873M market cap on $254M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $80M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 48% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of CCBG and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/Behavioral_Patterns_of_CCBG_and_Institutional_Flows_111026091602_1794320162.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794320162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Mirae Asset Global Investments Co. Ltd. Purchases 13,048 Shares of Capital City Bank Group $CCBG","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/mirae-asset-global-investments-co-ltd-purchases-13048-shares-of-capital-city-bank-group-ccbg.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794218012.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.961,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Capital City Bank Group (CCBG) vs. Its Competitors Head-To-Head Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/capital-city-bank-group-ccbg-vs-its-competitors-head-to-head-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793805308.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(CCBG) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/CCBG_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_103126101202_1793455922.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793455922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Contrasting California BanCorp (NASDAQ:BCAL) and Capital City Bank Group (NASDAQ:CCBG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"ht